==Icelandic==
===Etymology===
Old Norse
===Preposition===
'''með''' (+ {{accusative}}/ + {{dative}})

# [[with]]
#* '''1928''', [[w:is:Krummavísa|Krummavísa]] (“Raven Song”, on the [[w:source:Krummavísa|Icelandic Wikisource]]) by [[w:Jón Ásgeirsson|Jón Ásgeirsson]]
#*: ''Krummi krunkar úti,''
#*: ''kallar á nafna sinn:''
#*: ''„Ég fann höfud af hrúti'' 
#*: ''hrygg og gæruskinn.“''
#*: ''Komdu nú og kroppaðu '''með''' mér,''
#*: ''krummi nafni minn.''
#*:: “Krummi croaks outside,
#*:: calling his namesake: 
#*:: ‘I found the head of a ram, 
#*:: backbone and sheepskin.’ 
#*:: Come now and peck '''with''' me, 
#*:: Krummi, my namesake.”
#: ''Ég fór þangað '''með''' konunni minni.''
#:: I went there '''with''' my wife.

